-J-Xmx8g
-J-Xms4g
# One sbt JVM keeps every module's compiler and test class loaders it has used, and a CI job that
# tests many modules in one session (streaming, the Kafka connectors, protobuf, connect, ...)
# compiles connect against the Varka-sized sql modules late in that session. At 1g it ran out of
# Metaspace there; sbt itself advises against a limit, so this one is only a ceiling.
-J-XX:MaxMetaspaceSize=2g

# The Varka engine's kernels are compiled against the incubating Vector API, and zinc extracts
# a compiled Java class's API by loading it in this JVM - which needs the module too, or the
# `sql/varka/engine` compile fails with NoClassDefFoundError on jdk.incubator.vector.
-J--add-modules=jdk.incubator.vector
